   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "נִסְדַּק, נִיקַּב. תָּנֵי עוּלָּא בַּר חֲנִינָא: נִיקַּב נֶקֶב מְפוּלָּשׁ — בְּמַשֶּׁהוּ, וְשֶׁאֵינוֹ מְפוּלָּשׁ — בִּכְאִיסָּר.",
   "en": "The mishna continues discussing the halakha of an etrog that was «split» or «pierced. Ulla bar Ḥanina taught:» An etrog that was «pierced with a hole that» completely «goes through» its body is unfit «with any» size hole. If «the hole does not» completely «go through» the etrog, it is unfit only «with» a hole «the size of an issar» coin."
  }
 ],
